1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
FastAgentFactory is a local-first multi-agent platform
powered by an AMD Radeon GPU through ROCm.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
This demonstration follows one real task from the command line
and graphical interface to a complete user-facing result.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The inference node is online, and the AMD implementation
of llama.cpp is active.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:50,000
The system reports a gfx1100 Radeon GPU, ROCm 7.2,
three inference slots, and a loaded Qwen chat model.

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Three U.S. equity specialists cover market conditions,
company research, and portfolio risk.

6
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Their tools combine Yahoo Finance prices, SEC disclosures,
and transparent historical risk calculations.

7
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:32,000
I will submit one request covering Apple, Microsoft,
and NVIDIA over approximately 250 trading days.

8
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:46,000
It also requests portfolio estimates under five-percent
and ten-percent S&P 500 declines.

9
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The primary agent identifies available specialists
and decomposes the request into independent workstreams.

10
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Independent tasks execute concurrently, while final synthesis
waits for the required results.

11
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Runtime capacity follows the live llama.cpp slots
instead of a fixed worker limit.

12
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Every tool result preserves its provider, observation time,
warnings, and methodology boundaries.

13
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:56,000
During execution, Radeon telemetry remains visible
as the local model processes each workstream.

14
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:10,000
AgentPackages use separate workspaces and runtime directories
while sharing versioned, read-only dependency profiles.

15
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:24,000
The primary agent consolidates the evidence
into one structured Markdown report.

16
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:38,000
The report includes concentration, volatility, drawdown,
S&P 500 beta, correlation, and both stress scenarios.

17
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:52,000
It also identifies anomalies and separates historical
measurements from scenario estimates.

18
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The final delivery records sources, timestamps,
methodology limitations, and a financial-risk disclaimer.

19
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:20,000
This is real multi-agent execution on AMD Radeon hardware,
from one graphical request to a complete delivery.
